@startuml
title POST /api/ai-agents-teams/runs/{run_id}/commands/prepare + /send — revision-fenced durable command
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Authorized actor" as Actor #FFD8C2
participant "AgentsTeamsApiSdk\n.command(runId, req)" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "AgentsTeamsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3node\nchain + observer" as Chain #FFE4A6

Actor -> SDK : command(runId, { type, expected_revision,\n  wait_id?, payload?, ... })

group Phase 1 — prepare (mints the command; deploys nothing)
SDK -> API : POST .../runs/{run_id}/commands/prepare
API -> Domain : prepare command
Domain -> Domain : mint command_id; classify the\ncommand; build the encrypted\ncommand artifact; render the\nclaim contract; compute command\ncontent and capability hashes
Domain --> API : RunCommandResp { command_id,\n  command_class, target_wait_id?,\n  contract, issued_at, hashes }
API --> SDK : PrepareResponse { response, token }
end

group Sign and send — byte-exact echo required
SDK -> SDK : signed = signContract(contract, privateKey)
SDK -> API : POST .../commands/send\n{ prepare_request (byte-identical),\n  prepare_response, request: signed, token }
API -> API : verify the echo hash binding;\ncross-check the signed public claim\nagainst the encrypted command artifact
API -> Domain : deploy claim and await finality
Domain -> Chain : deploy signed command claim
Chain --> Domain : finalized
alt claim wins at expected_revision
  Chain --> Domain : command applied;\nrevision advanced
else stale revision (CAS loses)
  Chain --> Domain : command deploys but does not apply;\nrevision unchanged
end
Domain -> Chain : observer readback of the run ledger
Chain --> Domain : run-state JSON
API <-- Domain : run-state JSON
SDK <-- API : 200 (untyped run-state readback)
SDK --> Actor : { prepareResponse, sendResponse }
end

note over API #FFF0C7
Authorization is adjudicated by the on-chain
command ledger: the run owner and the configured
Embers service hold run-level authority; a
delegated approver may decide exactly the wait
named in their grant. A stale expected_revision
is not an HTTP error — the readback shows the
unchanged revision; refresh and re-issue.
end note
@enduml
